DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: luff and slew the boom, then hoist and pay out the independent rope-hung load.
# Model: Crane. Motor A turns the turntable: an 8-tooth gear on the 28-tooth turntable, so
# 315 degrees of the motor are a quarter turn of the crane (90 x 28 / 8 = 315).
# Motor B turns the spindle of a small linear actuator one to one (360 degrees push 1.2 mm);
# the actuator pushes the boom up. 1800 degrees lift the boom from 30 to about 60 degrees,
# and the rope guide at its tip rises about 4 cm. The actuator holds the boom when B stops.
# Motor C drives a 1:1 16T pair and a 7 LDU rope drum. Counterclockwise winds in;
# 540 degrees take in 7 x 0.4 x 3 x pi = 26.4 mm of rope at a stationary boom.
# Four pinned diagonal feet resist motor reaction torque; the base remains free on the floor.
# Clockwise pays it back out. The load can swing and the rope can go slack.
WHEN flag clicked:
  set motor stop action A hold
  stop motor A
  set motor stop action B hold
  stop motor B
  set motor stop action C hold
  stop motor C
  set motor speed A 10
  set motor speed B 100
  set motor speed C 100
  run motor B clockwise 1800 degrees
  wait 1 seconds
  run motor A clockwise 315 degrees
  wait 2 seconds
  run motor B counterclockwise 1800 degrees
  wait 1 seconds
  run motor A counterclockwise 315 degrees
  run motor C counterclockwise 540 degrees
  wait 0.5 seconds
  run motor C clockwise 540 degrees
  wait 0.5 seconds
